\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Quality-privacy trade-off across methods. The x-axis shows specific value recovery rate (lower is better for privacy) and the y-axis shows BERTScore F1 (higher is better for quality). Our pipeline and the entity substitution baseline are measured on CUAD; DP method recovery rates are from Pang et al.\nonbreakingspace \citep  {pang2024} with quality values estimated from the literature (not measured on CUAD). The green-shaded area marks the target zone below 10\% recovery.}}{6}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scatter}{{3}{6}{Quality-privacy trade-off across methods. The x-axis shows specific value recovery rate (lower is better for privacy) and the y-axis shows BERTScore F1 (higher is better for quality). Our pipeline and the entity substitution baseline are measured on CUAD; DP method recovery rates are from Pang et al.~\cite {pang2024} with quality values estimated from the literature (not measured on CUAD). The green-shaded area marks the target zone below 10\% recovery}{figure.caption.28}{}}
